  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Robbie Ray lasted 2.1 innings and the Yankees scored five. That's the game.",
    "what_this_means": "Ray couldn't hold the edge. By the second inning, Texas had pushed across four runs. The damage done before anyone with a Padres uniform got warm. The bullpen that followed was immaculate: Canning, Peralta, Morgan, Brito combined for 5.2 scoreless innings with eight strikeouts. It didn't matter. The offense managed three hits and twelve strikeouts. Manny Machado hit a solo shot. The only run they'd get. Four runners left in scoring position, four empty at-bats. They chased from the second inning forward and never caught up. This is a team built to win tight games where pitching matters. Today, the pitching couldn't start the game, and the bats never showed.",
